                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers [/h1]\n\nWhat a long, strange trip .... I have no idea what I just played, but I think I like it. Warning though: this game has been in Early Access since March 23, 2017 and it seems to be abandonware. The game as is has several bugs. I'm really giving a neutral recommendation at the sale price of $4.99, simply for the weird experience. \n\nThe bug I experienced was a missing key I had put in my inventory. I simply restarted the game and next time just held on to the key with my hand. I was unable to progress when the key vanished from my inventory. I don't even know why the game has an inventory to be honest. I also experienced a pathing issue, which I resolved by simply crouching and then I was able to move again.\n\nI got stuck on what I believe is the 2nd or perhaps it is the 3rd level. It is after you take the elevator all the way to the top. I ate all the mushrooms. I slept in the bed. I walked around all the areas. I have no idea how to progress. That left a bad taste in my mouth, no doubt. But I'm still not giving a negative recommendation, why?\n\nBecause as I stated, it was a long, strange trip. I love the music. I loved the little animations that seemingly randomly happened upon stumbling to some location / object. This is an absolutely beautiful world that you just want to explore because you want to see what is next. I took the weirdest bath. I ate all the shrooms. I hallucinated all kinds of things.\n\nRate 5/10. It's kind of sad that this game has been abandoned. WIth some work, it could be a unique, magical game / experience that only VR can bring.",
